  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the protestor as the speaker of the hateful text",
  "description": "The meme uses the deictic pronoun 'me' in the overlaid text 'helped me fish out all the mentally ill on my friends list' to project the user (the viewer of the meme) onto the protestor (the woman holding the 'OBAMA PRIDE' sign). The protestor is visually positioned as the agent performing the action described in the text, creating an analogical mapping where the user is identified with the protestor as the speaker of the hateful statement. This projection is reinforced by the visual framing of the protestor as the central figure in the scene, making her the implied 'me' in the text.",
